{
  "id": "PPA-11",
  "title": "Protein Quality Control & Turnover",
  "subtitle": "Endoplasmic reticulum folding, ubiquitin E1-E2-E3 conjugation, 26S proteasome, and autophagy",
  "caption": "Cellular protein homeostasis, refolding, and degradation machinery. Nascent polypeptide chains are folded in the ER lumen by BiP chaperones, calreticulin, and protein disulfide isomerases (PDI). Misfolded or regulatory proteins undergo targeted ubiquitination via sequential E1-E2-E3 cascades (including cullin-RING E3 ligases) and are degraded by the ATP-dependent 26S proteasome. Large protein aggregates and damaged organelles are sequestered into autophagosomes via the ATG8 core conjugation machinery for vacuolar lytic turnover.",
  "species_anchor": "arabidopsis_thaliana",
